extend type Query {
  """Read a directed belt component from one shared entity reference."""
  beltRun(target: EntityRefInput!, maxEntities: Int! = 1000): BeltRun!
  """One engine snapshot of selected-force machines, belts, chests, inserters and fluid entities intersecting an area, plus every surface inserter targeting those entities. Area dimensions must be positive and at most 256 tiles. Boundary edges retain actual outside endpoints; no distance-based connections are inferred."""
  factoryGraph(area: FactoryAreaInput!, force: String! = "player", surface: String! = "nauvis"): FactoryGraph!
  """Geometric adjacency of selected-force entities inside an area, verified against engine connections. Pairs include entities whose axis-aligned bounding boxes are at most tolerance tiles apart; connection is empty when they only touch or lie near each other without an engine connection (the usual misaligned pipe, boiler or inserter case). Underground and linked belt partners are engine connections, not geometric ones, and appear in factoryGraph instead. Area dimensions must be positive and at most 64 tiles; limit bounds both nodes and pairs."""
  adjacency(area: FactoryAreaInput!, force: String! = "player", surface: String! = "nauvis", tolerance: Float! = 0.5, limit: Int! = 1000): AdjacencyGraph!
}

extend type InspectionLogistics {
  surface: String!
  """Belt components reached from this inspection's actual inserter pickup/drop targets, read together in a new snapshot. Seeds already returned by a previous component are skipped; truncated components can overlap. Each traversal is bounded to maxEntities (1 through 1000). A changed or removed parent target is an error."""
  beltRuns(maxEntities: Int! = 1000): [BeltRun!]! @goField(forceResolver: true)
}

"""Directed structural connection, not measured item flow. kind is belt, underground, linked, loader, pickup, drop, or fluid. boundary means at least one endpoint lies outside the returned node set. Transport-line connections are collapsed to entity edges; splitter priorities and lane routing do not imply measured throughput. Fluid edges follow directed engine pipe connections, including pipes, boilers, pumps, offshore pumps, heat exchangers, storage tanks and fluid-consuming machines."""
type TopologyEdge {
  from: LogisticsEndpoint!
  to: LogisticsEndpoint!
  kind: String!
  boundary: Boolean!
  """Raw engine pipe-connection direction for fluid edges: input, output or input-output. Null for every other kind. Each connected port reports its own connection, so the same fluid pair can appear twice with mirrored endpoints and directions; use kind and endpoint identity for connectivity, not direction, to infer physical flow."""
  flowDirection: String
}

"""One bounded weakly connected belt component. Sources/sinks have no engine belt predecessor/successor, including checked connections beyond the traversal boundary. They are structural terminals, never stalled/dead-end diagnoses. Inserters are actual engine pickup/drop targets touching returned belts. Nodes can span surfaces through linked belts. Boundary edges describe omitted connected belts when truncated."""
type BeltRun {
  tick: Float!
  surface: String!
  seed: LogisticsEndpoint!
  maxEntities: Int!
  truncated: Boolean!
  nodes: [LogisticsEndpoint!]!
  edges: [TopologyEdge!]!
  boundaryEdges: [TopologyEdge!]!
  sources: [LogisticsEndpoint!]!
  sinks: [LogisticsEndpoint!]!
  inserters: [ConnectedInserter!]!
}

"""All supported selected-force nodes intersecting area, without pagination or silent omission. Supported machines: assembling machines, furnaces, drills, labs, rocket silos. Chests include logistic, linked, and infinity containers. Inserters also include outside-area and other-force inserters whose actual target is a returned node. Edges include physical belt, loader/container, and inserter pickup/drop connections. boundaryEdges are the subset crossing the returned node set, including force boundaries; endpoints remain fully identified. No adjacency guessing or rate estimates."""
type FactoryGraph {
  tick: Float!
  surface: String!
  force: String!
  area: WorldArea!
  nodes: [LogisticsEndpoint!]!
  machines: [LogisticsEndpoint!]!
  belts: [LogisticsEndpoint!]!
  chests: [LogisticsEndpoint!]!
  inserters: [ConnectedInserter!]!
  """Fluid-network entities in the area: offshore pumps, pipes, pipe-to-ground, pumps, boilers, generators, heat exchangers and storage tanks."""
  fluidEntities: [LogisticsEndpoint!]!
  edges: [TopologyEdge!]!
  boundaryEdges: [TopologyEdge!]!
}

"""Geometric adjacency inside an area, with engine verification. Nodes are all selected-force entities intersecting the area except characters, units, robots, corpses, items and ghosts. Pairs are unordered, each listed once, and only cover returned nodes; duplicate or self pairs never appear. Tracing item or fluid flow still needs factoryGraph edges, beltRun or fluidNetwork."""
type AdjacencyGraph {
  tick: Float!
  surface: String!
  force: String!
  area: WorldArea!
  tolerance: Float!
  limit: Int!
  """True when more nodes or pairs matched than the limit returned."""
  truncated: Boolean!
  nodes: [LogisticsEndpoint!]!
  pairs: [AdjacencyPair!]!
}

"""Bounding-box adjacency of two entities. gap is the shortest distance between axis-aligned bounding boxes in tiles, 0 when they touch or overlap. connection is the engine connection kind when the pair is actually connected (belt, underground, linked, loader, pickup, drop, fluid) and an empty string when the pair is only geometrically close or touching. Geometric adjacency never proves a belt, pipe or inserter will move items or fluid."""
type AdjacencyPair {
  a: LogisticsEndpoint!
  b: LogisticsEndpoint!
  connection: String!
  gap: Float!
}
